// Rate-of-change momentum (Pine: ta.roc(close, 10) > 5).
// ROC = percent change of close over the lookback window.
// REGIME: trend or expansion. Do NOT fire in chop - in a range a 5 percent
// 10-bar move marks the top of the range, so this becomes buy-the-high.
// CONDITIONS: range expanding, higher highs on the timeframe above.
// INVALIDATION: ROC decaying back under the threshold while price stalls
// (momentum exhaustion), or the whole move coming from one spike bar.
// SHAPE: 1h; a sustained directional push, not a single candle.
// NOT macd_histogram_flip: that signals a change of trend, this one signals
// continuation of a trend already running.
// CALIBRATED ON: crypto, 1h. The threshold is the danger here - a 5 percent
// move over 10 bars is an ordinary afternoon for BTC and a limit-move event
// for an index future. Do not carry the number across instrument classes.
strategy RocMomentum {

    every 1h {

        if ROC(10) > 5 {

            buy(BTCUSD, 0.7)

        }

    }

}
